From 3c918638b21ecedc288619a96ec19cdacf3d773a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mabn <github@mabn.pl>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:55:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 155/156] [barreplay] H126: the map work also in four bands of
 map rows

An 8v8 has two ally teams (three with Gaia), so (type, ally team) tasks halve
the heaviest type's map work at best. A span of an instance's squares lies
within one row (AddSquaresToInstance builds them row by row, of in-map
squares only) and a circle is added row by row, so a map splits into bands of
rows that never share a counter: each (type, ally team, band) task applies the
spans starting in its band and the circle rows inside it, skipping whole any
instance whose rows miss the band. The adds use the counter loop alone: in
full view the visible add's report of squares entering LOS returns at once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
